\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Equal spacing matches the scalar lattice}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{Let #{S} be the set of #{N=2M} equally spaced points on the
circle, with #{M\ge 2}. Every arc has length #{1/N}. The edge
weight in \ref{fdip-00FP} equals #{m/\sinh(m/N)} at every
edge, and the diagonal excess equals #{2m\tanh(m/(2N))} at
every site. The quadratic form is then the energy of
\ref{fdip-007O} for a one-point spatial factor and time cycle
of length #{N}, with every edge weight equal to
#{m/\sinh(m/N)} and with the on-site coefficient equal to the
diagonal excess #{2m\tanh(m/(2N))}.
The reflection #{x\mapsto -x} is the [site reflection](fdip-007M).
The half decomposition in \ref{fdip-00FP} is the lattice
decomposition of \ref{fdip-007O}, with a product series on each
arc joining a point to its image. The [finite-range circle precision](fdip-00C8) allows a
negative coefficient #{c_r}. The weights in \ref{fdip-00FP}
are the positive quantities #{m/\sinh(m h_i)} of the arc
precision.}
